Generate a cohesive set of three standalone graphic assets for the Urkaaaz
Loadout selection cards. These replace the current vector-drawn selected
frame, check badge, and information button. Match the attached selected-card
reference: a near-perimeter luminous gold frame and an oversized dark circular
check medallion overlapping its upper-right corner. Do not generate a screen
mockup or combine the assets into one image.

## Reference inputs

- Attach the user's screenshot of the selected unit card with the bright gold
  frame and check medallion. This is the primary visual reference for the
  frame's edge placement, glow, gold/bronze contrast, badge size, and overlap.
- Attach the current Loadout card screenshot only to communicate the actual
  app card's boundaries and content. Do not copy its current vector treatment.
- Attach one approved Urkaaaz unit-card illustration and the main-menu
  background as secondary palette and material references.
- The approved transparent lock image at
  `assets_src/loadout/ui/loadout_card_locked.png` is a separate availability
  overlay supplied by the user. Do not regenerate it or incorporate it into
  any of the three requested assets.
- Preserve the reference's brighter, cleaner gold treatment: a luminous
  yellow-gold rim, dark bronze edge/shadow, warm ivory highlights, and a
  visible amber glow. Do not substitute a flat yellow line or a bulky,
  ornamental frame.

## Shared art direction

- Create three independent transparent PNG assets that read clearly at small
  mobile-card sizes.
- Match the attached reference's metallic depth, contrast, outline weight,
  roundness, and warm glow. Keep the three assets in one coherent visual
  family, not generic flat icons.
- Keep the structural edges crisp and the glow soft. The bright gold should
  remain visible over the supplied unit art, including bright sky areas.
- Use transparent backgrounds. Do not include a card image, screenshot,
  panel, scenery, text label, or any UI beyond the individual requested asset.
- The semi-transparent unit-title strip and its live Cinzel SemiBold label
  are rendered separately by Android; do not include them in any of these
  three asset files.
- Keep edge glow inside the image bounds; do not rely on content outside the
  PNG canvas.
- Do not introduce game logos, faction symbols, invented currency, or
  decorative details that obscure the function of the asset.

## Asset 1: selected card frame

- Output filename: `loadout_selected_frame.png`
- Canvas: exactly 512 x 720 pixels, RGBA PNG.
- Draw a complete portrait-card frame with a fully transparent center.
- The frame must closely follow the card's perimeter. Keep its visible
  structural rim about 3-5% inward from the canvas edge, matching the
  reference; do not leave a wide transparent margin that makes it appear
  smaller than the illustration.
- Reproduce the reference's continuous bright yellow-gold rim: a narrow
  luminous inner highlight, a warm saturated gold body, a dark bronze outer
  bevel/shadow, and a soft amber glow around the edge. Keep the edge weight
  balanced and consistent on all four sides.
- Use rounded corners matching the portrait card. Keep them smooth,
  symmetrical, and close to the reference. Do not add corner medallions,
  rivets, gemstones, arrows, symbols, or extra ornaments.
- The entire interior must remain transparent, including any space between
  the inner rim and the unit illustration. Do not add a tint or panel fill.
- Do not include a check badge; it is a separate overlay.

## Asset 2: selected check badge

- Output filename: `loadout_selected_badge.png`
- Canvas: exactly 256 x 256 pixels, RGBA PNG.
- Create the reference's prominent circular medallion: a dark, nearly black
  brown center, a thick luminous yellow-gold ring, warm ivory-gold highlights,
  and a clearly readable centered check.
- Give the badge a soft, strong amber halo. Its gold rim should remain visible
  while overlapping the selected frame and bright card art.
- The badge is positioned by Android so it overlaps the card frame at the
  upper-right corner, as in the reference. Draw the complete circle and its
  glow inside this standalone asset; do not draw any part of the card frame.
- Keep the check mark bold and unmistakable at small size. Do not use the
  letter "V" as a substitute.
- Keep the badge centered with a small transparent safety margin for its
  glow. Do not add text, numbers, stars, or secondary symbols.

## Asset 3: information button

- Output filename: `loadout_info_icon.png`
- Canvas: exactly 256 x 256 pixels, RGBA PNG.
- Create a circular information button with a dark, nearly black brown
  center, a luminous yellow-gold rim, warm ivory-gold highlights, and a
  centered lowercase "i" glyph.
- Match the selected badge's metal, lighting, contrast, and glow, but keep
  this control visually distinct from the larger check medallion.
- Keep the glyph simple and crisp at small size. No words, labels, question
  marks, check marks, or other symbols.
- Keep the button centered with a small transparent safety margin for its
  glow.

## Negative requirements

- No opaque background, checkerboard, card mockup, illustration, screenshot,
  text, labels, extra controls, logo, watermark, signature, or contact sheet.
- No inset frame with a wide transparent border; the selected frame must
  follow the near-perimeter placement in the reference.
- No flat yellow strokes, default platform icons, thin unreadable marks,
  excessive bloom, jagged outlines, bulky ornate trim, asymmetric frame, or
  uneven corners.
- Do not place the check badge or information icon inside the frame image.

## Output and review

Return exactly three independent PNG files with the exact filenames,
dimensions, and alpha transparency specified above. Save them for review under:

```text
assets_src/loadout/ui/
```

Before delivery, verify that:

- all three files are valid RGBA PNGs with the exact specified dimensions;
- the frame alpha channel is transparent throughout its center and its rim
  follows the near-perimeter inset shown in the reference;
- the badge and information icon remain distinct and legible when reduced to
  their small on-card sizes, with the badge visually larger and more luminous;
- the frame, badge, and information icon match the reference's bright
  yellow-gold, dark bronze, and warm amber treatment;
- no asset contains any unintended text, background, UI, or watermark.

Show all three assets on both a dark and a bright card background for visual
approval. Do not integrate them into Android resources until approved.
